  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Fiji Carbon Budget and Fossil Fuel Subsidy Policy Reform</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="4">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Active</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The main objective of this project is to support Fiji&apos;s transition to a low-emissions and climate-resilient development pathway through better planning and informed decision-making. The project will accelerate domestic action on mitigation priorities. The carbon budget component will enable Fiji to strategically manage its trajectory toward its Net Zero by 2050 target by setting a clear legal and methodological foundation. The fossil fuel reform component aims to ensure a more efficient and better-targeted use of government finances. By reducing reliance on unsustainable subsidies, the project strengthens public funds available for critical climate action and investment, building resilience across key sectors.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This dual-component project supports the implementation of Fiji&#x2019;s Climate Change Act 2021 by developing the nation&#x2019;s First 5-year Carbon Budget (2026-2030) and accelerating Fossil Fuel Subsidy Reform . The carbon budget component involves three phases, starting with recommending a methodological approach and collecting data . This is followed by developing an indicative budget by mid-2023 and finalizing the Updated Carbon Budget by December 2023 . The subsidy reform component will first prioritize and design the reform through the creation of a Roadmap . This Roadmap will then be implemented through technical support for government approval processes and stakeholder engagement, aiming for policy change by September 2024 .</narrative>
  </description>
